# Cursor Rules & Agent Harness Directives

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/WORKFLOW.md` as primary authority.

## Non-Negotiable Rules:
1. Empirical Metrics Only: Always cite exit codes, test outputs, and compiler logs.
2. Strict TDD: Write failing test (RED) before writing code (GREEN).
3. Gates Enforcement: Follow `.agents/rules/ecc-harness-gate.md`.
4. Headless Browsers Only: Never launch headed browser windows (`headless: true`).
5. Durable Plans: Multi-step work belongs in `docs/plans/active/`.
6. Auto-Experience Journaling: Append defect root-cause & lessons into `docs/memory/failure-journal.md` upon completion.
7. Zero-Drop & Multi-Goal: Extract Goal Matrix for multi-issue prompts, run negative boundary tests, and verify full suite before reporting.
8. Zero-Emoji UI: Never use emojis as icons; mandate Lucide/Heroicons SVG and high-end neutral zinc/slate palette.
9. Autonomous Research: Never hallucinate APIs; inspect via `gh` CLI, `search_web`, or `scripts/inspect-package.ps1`.
